{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================
  Wishlist row — one saved product
  ============================================================

  Fetched with Shopify's Section Rendering API, one request per saved item:

      /products/{handle}?section_id=sp-wishlist-item

  WHY FETCH AT ALL, when the browser already knows what was saved?

  Because the only thing worth storing locally is WHICH products were saved,
  never what they cost. A price cached at save time is a price that goes
  stale — the shopper comes back a month later and the drawer quotes them a
  figure the shop no longer honours. Everything perishable (price, sale
  status, availability, money format, translation) is rendered here, by the
  same Liquid the product page uses, at the moment the drawer opens.

  localStorage holds the id and the handle. Nothing else.
  ============================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  assign on_sale = false
  if v.compare_at_price > v.price
    assign on_sale = true
  endif

  comment
    Quick-add is only offered where there is genuinely nothing to choose.
    A one-click add on a product with fabric options would be picking the
    shopper's fabric for them.
  endcomment
  assign single = false
  if product.variants.size == 1 and v.available
    assign single = true
  endif

  comment
    A product whose variants differ in price would otherwise show one bare
    figure — the cheapest — as if it were the price. Formatting has to happen
    BEFORE the translation is applied: `t` returns a finished string, so
    piping money afterwards would print the raw pennies.
  endcomment
  assign price_display = v.price | money
  if product.price_varies
    assign cheapest = product.price_min | money
    assign price_display = 'products.product.price.from_price_html' | t: price: cheapest
  endif
-%}

<div class="sp-wl__item" data-sp-wl-item>
  <a class="sp-wl__media" href="{{ product.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- if product.featured_media -%}
      {%- assign m_alt = '' -%}
      {{
        product.featured_media
        | image_url: width: 300
        | image_tag: class: 'sp-wl__img', widths: '120, 200, 300', sizes: '84px', loading: 'lazy', alt: m_alt
      }}
    {%- else -%}
      <span class="sp-wl__ph"></span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </a>

  <div class="sp-wl__detail">
    <div class="sp-wl__head">
      <div class="sp-wl__copy">
        {%- if product.vendor != blank -%}
          <p class="sp-wl__vendor">{{ product.vendor | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <a class="sp-wl__name" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a>
      </div>

      <button
        type="button"
        class="sp-wl__remove"
        data-sp-wl-remove="{{ product.id }}"
        aria-label="{{ 'sections.cart.remove_title' | t: title: product.title }}"
      >
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>

    <p class="sp-wl__prices">
      <span class="sp-wl__now">{{ price_display }}</span>
      {%- if on_sale and product.price_varies == false -%}
        <s class="sp-wl__was">{{ v.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>

    {%- if product.available -%}
      {%- if single -%}
        {%- form 'product', product, class: 'sp-wl__form', novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ v.id }}">
          <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
          <button type="submit" class="sp-wl__add" data-sp-quickadd>
            {{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}
          </button>
        {%- endform -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Deliberately a link to the product page, not the quick view. The
          quick view is itself an overlay, and stacking one on top of this
          drawer would leave the shopper two layers deep with two close
          buttons. Choosing a fabric is a considered act — the product page
          is the right place for it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <a class="sp-wl__add sp-wl__add--options" href="{{ product.url }}">
          {{ 'products.product.choose_options' | t }}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="sp-wl__soldout">{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Wishlist row",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
